    o := other.(*threadSafeSet[T])
    // ...
}
```

It has the same issue! And in threadUnsafeSet:
```go
func (s *threadUnsafeSet[T]) Equal(other Set[T]) bool {
    o := other.(*threadUnsafeSet[T])
    // ...
}
```

But looking at the IsSubset method in threadUnsafeSet:
```go
func (s *threadUnsafeSet[T]) IsSubset(other Set[T]) bool {
    // Uses other.Contains() without type assertion
}
```

So some methods correctly use the interface methods while others incorrectly use type assertions.

